(2) Serve as the ceremonial head of the city and as its official representative to federal, state, and local governmental bodies and officials and to be the official spokesperson for the city council and the chief advocate of city council policies;
(3) Recommend to the councilmembers such measures relative to the affairs of the city, improvement of the government, and promotion of the welfare of its inhabitants as such officer may deem expedient;
(4) Administer oaths and take affidavits;
(5) Execute all contracts, deeds, and other obligations of the city within a level of authorization as established by the city council; and
(6) Vote on matters before the city council to the extent provided in subsection (a) of Section 2.10 of this charter.

